From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:59:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: mt6789: Drop the unused EH driving table

The common pinctrl-paris code has no EH (I2C high-drive) register class,
so mt6789_pin_eh_range was never referenced and W=1 builds warn about
it. Remove the table and the commented-out reference to it; it can come
back with EH support in the common code.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c | 38 -----------------------
 1 file changed, 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
index b4c58209..408c1709 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
@@ -1073,43 +1073,6 @@ static const struct mtk_pin_field_calc mt6789_pin_drv_range[] = {
 	PIN_FIELD_BASE(187, 187, 4, 0x0060, 0x10, 18, 3),
 };
 
